Author: ollie <ohoidn>
Date:   Thu Dec 4 01:34:02 2025 -0800

    ARCH-SIM-CONSTRUCTION-001: Fix SQUARE lattice sincg precision (SIM-CONSTR-PARTIALITY-001)
    
    Upcast fractional HKL deltas (h-h0, k-k0, l-l0) to float64 before sincg
    evaluation to preserve (Na·Nb·Nc)² lattice weight scaling near integer
    Miller indices. Float32 underflows cause sincg to return incorrect values
    when delta ≈ 0, collapsing the expected partiality boost.
    
    Changes:
    - simulator.py lines 299-315: compute deltas in float64, evaluate sincg,
      then downcast F_latt back to simulator dtype before combining with F_cell
    - Use torch.as_tensor() instead of torch.tensor() to handle both scalar
      and tensor N_cells inputs
    
    Contract: docs/spec-db-core.md:60-140 (lattice weights ∝ (Na·Nb·Nc)²)
    Finding: SIM-CONSTR-PARTIALITY-001
    Tag: nanobrag-partiality-2025-12-26
    
